# crafty publishing (library-and-publishing)

## Never do this on a real release

```bash
cargo publish --workspace   # ❌ bursts ~11 new crates → HTTP 429 on first release
```

Use **`./scripts/publish-workspace.sh`** (one crate at a time, skip indexed, retry 429).

## Release flow

```bash
# 1. CHANGELOG: move [Unreleased] → new version section
# 2. Prepare tag (dry-run gate + commit if bumped + tag)
./scripts/release.sh 0.2.0
git push && git push origin v0.2.0

# 3. Publish (after tag push; or CI manual job)
./scripts/release.sh 0.2.0 --publish-only
# commits post-publish docs separately — see skill
```

First release when manifest is already at target version: step 2 skips bump; step 3 uses `--publish-only` if tag exists.

## crates.io rate limits (first release)

| Fact | Implication |
|------|-------------|
| **New-crate burst limit** | ~5 uploads in quick succession → `429 Too Many Requests` |
| **`cargo publish --workspace`** | Uploads multiple new crates in one run → hits limit |
| **429 body** | Contains `try again after <RFC7231 date> GMT` — parse and wait |
| **Partial publish** | Re-running `cargo publish --workspace` fails with *already exists* |
| **Resume** | `./scripts/publish-workspace.sh` skips crates already at version on index |

Defaults: **30s** between successful uploads (`CRAFTY_PUBLISH_DELAY_SECS`), **5s** buffer after 429 retry time (`CRAFTY_PUBLISH_429_BUFFER_SECS`).

## Prerequisites

- `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN` or `cargo login`
- Clean tree for **prepare** (`release.sh` without `--publish-only`)
- Tag pushed before CI manual `publish` job

## CI

- Fast lane / tag `publish-dry-run`: `cargo publish --workspace --dry-run` (OK — no uploads)
- Tag manual `publish`: `./scripts/publish-workspace.sh` (not bare `--workspace`)

## Docs after publish

`post-publish-docs.sh` adds crates.io/docs.rs badges and updates `docs/status.md`. Run automatically via `release.sh --publish-only`; commit the diff.

See [docs/releasing.md](../../docs/releasing.md) and skill `.cursor/skills/crafty-publishing/`.
